

actor Airline -> pool AirlineClaimProcess

map RetrieveArrivalTimeFromBooking          -> node retrieveBookingTime
map RetrieveDoorOpenTime                    -> node retrieveDoorOpenTime
map CalculateDelayAtArrival                 -> node calculateDelay
map RetrieveInfoFromInternalSystems         -> node retrieveInternalSystemsInfo
map RegisterJudgementCriteriaAndTypeOfEC    -> node registerJudgementCriteria
map RecordJustificationForExclusion         -> node recordJustificationExclusionA
map ApproveCompensation                     -> node approveCompensation
map DenyCompensation                        -> node denyCompensation
map DocumentAndSaveFileCase                 -> node documentAndSaveFileCase

# Not mapped (silent BPMN routing steps, map(n) = epsilon):
#   start1, gw_split, gw_join, gw_afterCalc, gw_afterInfo, gw_afterRegister, end1
# Not mapped — duplicate occurrence in the source Petri net (see .bpmn2 header comment):
#   recordJustificationExclusionB is the SAME i* task (RecordJustificationForExclusion) reached
#   via a different branch (was mapped from t10, while recordJustificationExclusionA is t14) —
#   ElementMapping is 1:1, so only one BPMN occurrence can be the mapped node; the other is
#   left silent here. Re-map to B instead of A if the "extraordinary circumstance" branch
#   coming straight out of gw_afterCalc is the one you want to trace.
# Not mapped (i* elements satisfied only via AND/OR propagation, never directly):
